-- title:
--   Moving places centred off the j-chart to good points
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q\ge 5$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Write $\bar F =$ `fieldBar q M'` for the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}\subseteq$ `LaurentSeries` $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ obtained by base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H=$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; and write `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` for the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$, which by the hypothesis `hle` is contained in $\bar F$. Here a `Place` of a field extension is a valuation subring containing the image of the base field, different from the whole field and a principal ideal ring; `ord` is its associated $\mathbb Z$-valued order function, `IsRational` means that the base field surjects onto its residue field, and `evalAt f` is the base-field element representing the residue of $f$ when $f$ is in the valuation subring, and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   The data and hypotheses are as follows. A finset $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ is given, with `hW` asserting that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: those places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`, the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic Weierstrass curve with invariant $j$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `integers` of the source, a surjective ring homomorphism `residue` to the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, contracting to $A$ along the constants and compatible with the residue map of $A$, such that every nonzero element can be rescaled by a constant into `integers` with nonzero residue, together with a map `placeMap` on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of elements with nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Further, $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, the set of primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` denotes the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of $\bar F$ attached to a root of unity $\zeta'$ and $\gamma\in SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ by the $q$-expansion condition `IsLevelAutBar` (the identity if no such automorphism exists), and `redQ q` is the reduction $SL(2,\mathbb Z)\to GL_2(\mathbb Z/q)$ acting on the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$, with `lineInfty q` the point $[1:0]$.
--
--   Two families of valuation subrings of $\bar F$ are given: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by the projective line over $\mathbb Z/q$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. The Igusa group of hypotheses consists of: `hIg_inf`, which describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ as the Gauss-type ring of those $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ after coefficientwise inclusion; `hIg`, which provides for each line $\ell$ some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ carrying `lineInfty q` to $\ell$ under `redQ q` and with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which says that for every root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$. The supersingular group consists of: `hSS_A`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contracts to $A$ on constants; `hSS_over`, which for $s\in W$ and $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ has nonnegative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element $j$ (the image of the $q$-expansion `jq`) has nonnegative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, asserts that the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and that for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at the $R_0$-residue of $f$ the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is preserved by pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t$ minus the image of any $a\in A$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$.
--
--   Next, $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\bar F$ to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, that is, a valuation subring of $\bar F$ with a surjective residue map onto that field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, contracting to $A$ on constants, compatible with the residue map of $A$ and with the rescaling property; `hR` identifies $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and `hR₀O` says that an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when its image in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   The arithmetic data are: an element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian local, has algebraically closed residue field, and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hκ`); an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$, together with $\zeta_0\in k_0$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity and $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; and a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ that is the contraction of $A$ (`hA₁`) and is a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated with $\bar F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq\bar F$ subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\bar F$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness condition, namely for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar F$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$; and $F_0$ contains every element of $\bar F$ whose Laurent series comes from a Laurent series over $\mathbb Q$ (lies in the range of `coeffEmb`). Write $T_1$ for the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $\bar F$ generated by the image of $K_1$. Let $T_1$ carry an $A_1$-algebra structure for which the structure map agrees with the inclusion of $K_1$ into $\bar F$ through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $j_1\in T_1$ be an element whose image in $\bar F$ is the inclusion of the $q$-expansion of $j$ (the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by `coeffEmb` applied to `jq`), with $j_1\ne 0$. Let $\mathfrak X=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel` $A_1\,T_1\,j_1$, the pushout of the two maps from the middle chart to $X_{\mathrm{fin}}=\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` and $X_\infty=\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf`, where `chartAlgFin` (resp. `chartAlgInf`) is the subalgebra of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ (resp. $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$), and `toBase` is its structure map to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$.
--
--   The statement introduces abbreviations for points $x$ of $\mathfrak X$ and elements $f$ of $T_1$: `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ whose image under `ιFin` is $x$ there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h\notin y$ and $f\cdot h=g$, and likewise for $X_\infty$ with `chartAlgInf`; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g\in y$. For a place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational and that every $f\in T_1$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and satisfies: the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of five clauses: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; every $y$ with $x\rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$; for every $y$ in $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ over $x$, every $b\in$ `chartAlgFin` whose image in $\bar F$ is a non-unit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y$; the same for $X_\infty$ and `chartAlgInf`; and for every $y$ in $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j_1)$ (the image of the chart generator `jChartFin`) does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`. Two further abbreviations are introduced: `Reads x Q`, for a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, saying that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, has $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$, and this residue is a non-unit there exactly when `InMax x f`; and `OffBranch x`, saying that for each line $\ell\ne$ `lineInfty q` and each $y$ in $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ (resp. $X_\infty$) over $x$ there is an element of the corresponding chart algebra that is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ in $\bar F$ and does not lie in $y$.
--
--   The assertion is: for every place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X$ with `Centred P x`, if $x$ is not in the image of the base map of `ιFin`, then there exists $\gamma\in SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a point $x'$ of $\mathfrak X$ such that `GoodPt x'` holds and `Centred` holds for the transported place `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ • P` at $x'$.
--
--   This is the pole-chart half of the covering step used in constructing the smooth Igusa base model: a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-rational place centred at a point of the two-chart integral model that lies outside the finite ($j$-)chart is moved by a level automorphism attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ onto a point which is closed in the special fibre, lies on the $\infty$-Igusa branch and is not supersingular in the sense of the $j$-invariant clause. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube).
